KZ2 patch 6032 (diagnostic, LD_UPCHK=1): live-draw checks against upstream ps3recomp PRs #501, #502, #504 and #508.

The question: which of four upstream fixes for the shared Vulkan/Metal engine also apply to the D3D12 live
draw. With LD_UPCHK=1 the bind loop counts every depth-format texture bind (DEPTH24_D8/_FLOAT, DEPTH16/_FLOAT) by
format, CONTROL1 crossbar and serving path (zeta snapshot, zeta window of patch 2063, CPU decode, colour surface);
counts depth snapshots and zeta windows created and retired, the texture cache size and all textures retired (#502:
a per-frame leak shows as a growing live count); counts compressed (DXT) textures that matched a render target (#508);
and counts vertex fetches whose base + offset is at or past 0x10000000 (#504; fetch_attr here, the compact plan in
rsx_vertex_compact.c, which counts without the switch). A summary "[upchk]" line every 512 frames; first examples as
"[upchk] ex". Off: one cached getenv per bound unit.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (hand-merged): HEAD's rsx_dsp_resolve_vertex_offset plus the raw-sum diagnostic

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c b/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c
